WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:03.868
-Senate Republicans,
joined by Democrat Joe Manchin,

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:06.567
blocked a bill called the
Women's Health Protection Act

00:00:06.567 --> 00:00:09.634
that would codify abortion
rights at the Federal level.

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:13.200
Also, we found out yesterday
that when he was president,

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:18.434
Donald Trump asked his advisers
if China had a hurricane gun

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:20.801
that it was using
against the United States.

00:00:20.801 --> 00:00:22.033
Are those two things related?

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:23.601
I guess you'll have to stay
tuned to find out.

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:26.467
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:28.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.167
♪♪

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:33.934
Every time you think
you're heard the dumbest thing

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:35.667
Donald Trump said
or did as president,

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:37.234
he somehow finds
a way to shock you.

00:00:37.234 --> 00:00:39.467
I didn't even know I still had

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:41.467
the capacity
to be shocked by Trump.

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:45.200
It's like how, even after seven
seasons of shocking deaths

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:49.067
on "Game of Thrones," I still
gasped when Littlefinger died.

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:52.267
Oh, I mean, or he lived?

00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:53.834
I should have said
"spoiler alert,"

00:00:53.834 --> 00:00:55.901
but if you couldn't guess that
Littlefinger was going to die,

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:57.367
then maybe
"Game of Thrones" isn't for you.

00:00:57.367 --> 00:00:59.334
I mean, he had a goatee,
and he talked like this.

00:00:59.334 --> 00:01:02.367
[ Droning ] "Lady Sansa.

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:05.400
You can trust me, Lady Sansa."

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:06.934
[ Normal voice ] Now, it might
seem weird to be referencing

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:10.367
"Game of Thrones" now, but there
is a prequel coming out,

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:14.968
and baby Littlefinger is in it.
Littlerfinger.

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:17.033
Anyway, this has been
"The News Is Super Depressing

00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:18.300
So Seth Put A Goatee On A Baby."

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.133
[ Chime plays ]

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:22.033
The point is, I was still
shocked yesterday

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:24.701
when "Rolling Stone" reported
that Trump kept asking

00:01:24.701 --> 00:01:26.501
his advisors if China

00:01:26.501 --> 00:01:28.868
was shooting us
with a hurricane gun.

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:30.434
According to "Rolling Stone,"
near the beginning

00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:32.434
of Trump's time in office,
he had a pressing question

00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:34.601
for his national security aides
and administration officials --

00:01:34.601 --> 00:01:38.033
does China have the secret
technology, a weapon even,

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:40.801
to create large man-made
Hurricanes and then launch them

00:01:40.801 --> 00:01:42.033
at the United States?

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:44.767
And if so, would this constitute
an act of war

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:48.267
by a foreign power, and could
the U.S. retaliate militarily?

00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:50.434
Trump repeatedly asked about
this, according to two former

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:53.434
senior administration officials
and a third person

00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:55.000
briefed on the matter.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.767
And this was at the beginning
of his presidency,

00:01:57.767 --> 00:02:01.801
and somehow his presidency still
had a middle and an end.

00:02:01.801 --> 00:02:05.033
Can you imagine if you went
to Starbucks and ordered

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:08.033
and the barista said, "Uh-huh.
Now, what exactly is coffee?"

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:10.567
And then you went back four
years later,

00:02:10.567 --> 00:02:12.234
and that barista was the
manager.

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:14.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.734
Also, Trump is so [bleep]
crazy that he doesn't just ask,

00:02:16.734 --> 00:02:18.467
does China have a hurricane gun.

00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:21.400
He's got a bunch of follow-ups,
assuming the answer

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.601
is gonna be yes.

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:23.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.868 --> 00:02:25.667
How does he even get
to the follow-ups?

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:28.234
"Does China have
a hurricane gun? And if so --"

00:02:28.234 --> 00:02:30.133
"Actually, we can just jump
in right now

00:02:30.133 --> 00:02:31.234
and save you some time.

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:32.834
They do not have
a hurricane gun."

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:34.767
="Right, but if they did --"
"They don't."

00:02:34.767 --> 00:02:36.300
"Sure, but if they were to
develop one --"

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.434
"They won't."

00:02:37.434 --> 00:02:39.601
It's never just one question.

00:02:39.601 --> 00:02:41.167
It's a series of questions.

00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:43.367
I imagine him sitting
in a leather chair

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:46.200
with a smoking
jacket in the study,

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:50.501
Sherlock style, pondering the
implications of his discovery.

00:02:50.501 --> 00:02:51.934
[ As Sherlock Holmes ]
"Is it possible that China

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:55.234
is using a hurricane gun
to attack us?

00:02:55.234 --> 00:02:58.234
If that is the case, would the
use of such a weapon

00:02:58.234 --> 00:03:01.133
not constitute an act of war
against a sovereign country?

00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:04.167
And if, as international law
stipulates, a sovereign nation

00:03:04.167 --> 00:03:06.868
has the right to defend
itself when attacked

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:11.601
by an aggressor nation,
does that not then imply

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:15.000
that the logical response
would be to respond

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.133
with a weapon of our own?

00:03:16.133 --> 00:03:18.734
Perhaps, and I am merely
brainstorming here,

00:03:18.734 --> 00:03:20.267
a tornado cannon."

00:03:20.267 --> 00:03:23.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.267 --> 00:03:25.834
Maybe this explains
why he was so obsessed

00:03:25.834 --> 00:03:28.167
with how much water
there was in Hurricanes.

00:03:28.167 --> 00:03:32.000
He thought China was making them
extra wet on purpose.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.601
-This is a tough Hurricane,
one of the wettest

00:03:35.601 --> 00:03:38.801
we've ever seen, from the
standpoint of water.

00:03:38.801 --> 00:03:41.968
It's tremendously big
and tremendously wet.

00:03:41.968 --> 00:03:44.868
-Tremendously big
and tremendously wet.

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:46.734
I think that's playing
at the art house cinema

00:03:46.734 --> 00:03:47.801
near my apartment.

00:03:47.801 --> 00:03:49.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:52.367
It's French, though,
so I'm not sure.

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:54.934
Trump's unhinged conspiracy
theories matter,

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:57.200
because they are the core
of the modern GOP,

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.467
a party that has repeatedly said
Trump is their leader,

00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:03.167
and if they get their way, will
put Trump back in power in 2024,

00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:04.634
either by winning or finishing

00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:06.200
off the coup they started
in 2020.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:09.267
One of our two major political
parties is more concerned

00:04:09.267 --> 00:04:11.534
